# RUN: llc -mtriple=mncore2 %s -o - | FileCheck %s
#
# G0: matrix transport golden, f32, both halves of the X face.
#
# Bit-exact round trip with no floating point involved (fmwrite/fmread copy
# raw bits, SDM 3.6.10/3.6.11), so every physical cell is checked with a
# unique 32-bit pattern instead of a value:
#
#   slot k in the PE file (odd/even word pair), PE p:
#     k = 0..3 : longword ((0x20+k) << 32) | (0x10+p)      <- matrix rows 0..3
#     k = 4..7 : longword ((0x40+k) << 32) | (0x30+p)      <- matrix rows 4..7
#   row k column 2p   gets the longword's LOW  half
#   row k column 2p+1 gets the longword's HIGH half
#
# Both matrix instructions use the LONGWORD (width=1) packing: SDM 3.6.10 says
# fmwrite consumes one longword per PE per cycle (4 rows/instruction) and
# 3.6.11 says fmread produces one longword per PE per cycle (4 columns).
# Width 0 / 2 do not produce this mapping -- see design doc section 22.7
# (mncore_intrinsics_design.md, "G0 实测：矩阵搬运的物理落点").
#
# Verified measured map (gpfn3, 2026-11-04; scripts/check_mau_g0.py):
#   fmwrite  cycle c: source longword at (src_addr + 2c) words,
#                     matrix row (start_row + c) mod 8.
#   fmread   cycle c: matrix column (start_col + c),
#                     PE p receives rows 2p (HIGH word) and 2p+1 (LOW word),
#                     written to dst longword (dst_addr/2 + (c XOR 1)).
#
# d set/get spec: [3:0]mem (1=GRF0 6=L1B), [20:4]addr(word), [28:21]nwords
#   L1B@<a> n1 = 6 | (a << 4) | (1 << 21)
#   GRF0@0 n64 = 1 | (64 << 21)

--- |
  target triple = "mncore2"
  define void @mau_g0() { ret void }
...
---
